`{{stinger.rust.package_name}}` is generated Rust code for the **{{stinger.name}}** IPC
interface. It lets processes on the same machine — or anywhere that can reach the same
MQTT broker — talk to each other over a shared, strongly typed contract.

Nothing in this crate opens a socket of its own. You supply an MQTT client, and this
crate turns typed Rust calls into MQTT publishes, and incoming MQTT messages back into
typed Rust values.
