## Feature flags

The crate has no default features, so a consumer compiles only the half it needs.

| Feature | What it adds |
|---|---|
| `client` | The `client` module (`{{stinger.rust.client_struct_name}}`) and the `discovery` module. |
| `server` | The `server` module (`{{stinger.rust.server_struct_name}}`) and the method-handler trait. |
| `metrics` | Message and error counters on the client, server, and discovery objects. |
| `lwt` | MQTT Last Will and Testament support, for announcing that a process has dropped off. |

Payload types, enums, and structs are always compiled in, with or without features.

> **Building these docs:** because nothing is enabled by default, run
> `cargo doc --all-features --open` to see the client and server pages.

